Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pynput (>= 1.7), python3-pyqt6 (>= 6.0), python3-hid, libhidapi-hidraw0
Suggests: python3-pyyaml
Replaces: msi-monitor-ctl (<< 0.1.0)
Description: Modern system tray application for MSI monitor control on Linux
 Monicon provides a clean, modern interface for controlling MSI gaming monitors
 on Linux, featuring:
 .
  - System tray integration with context menus
  - Input source switching (HDMI, DisplayPort, USB-C)
  - Profile management and cycling
  - Global customizable keyboard shortcuts
  - Custom names for inputs and profiles
  - XDG-compliant configuration
  - Cross-desktop environment compatibility
 .
 Supports: Arch, Fedora, openSUSE, Debian/Ubuntu and other Linux distributions.
 Works on GNOME, KDE Plasma, XFCE, i3, and other desktop environments.
